    "parts": [],
    "answer_text": "Parenchyma: Living cells with thin walls, uniformly thin, loosely packed with large intercellular spaces. Collenchyma: Living cells with slightly thick walls, elongated, irregularly thickened at corners with very little intercellular spaces. Sclerenchyma: Dead cells with thick cell walls, long and narrow, thickened due to lignin with no internal space.",
